 # Pitfalls
 
-Status: empty template. No application or company facts have been admitted.
+Status: generated entries from the first maintenance run. They require human review.
 
 Use PIT IDs for evidence-backed entries, with explicit scope. Generated entries require human review. Implementation observations do not establish company policy.
 
 | ID | Trigger | What goes wrong | Do instead | Scope | Evidence |
 | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| PIT001 | Scaling a stored amount by a currency's decimalPlaces (e.g. 10^decimalPlaces), or giving a helper a decimalPlaces argument that changes the stored scale | The same value is read at different scales on different screens. A 1,500 yen budget showed as 15 on one screen and 150,000 on another, because useFormat and some util helpers used 10^decimalPlaces while the rest of the code used x100. | Store every amount at x100 for all currencies (1500 yen is 150000 in the DB). Use decimalPlaces only for display and input formatting. amountToInteger, integerToAmount and integerToCurrency take no decimalPlaces argument. | app:actual | Developer decision; `packages/loot-core/src/shared/util.ts` |
+| PIT002 | Typing into the legacy AmountInput with autoDecimals on, for a currency with no decimals (e.g. yen), when the field treats typed digits as cents | Typing 1500 shows 15.00 instead of 1500 whole units, so the value is wrong by a factor of 100. | Skip autoDecimals when the currency's decimalPlaces is 0 (guard `autoDecimals && format.currency.decimalPlaces > 0`). Keep the AmountInput tests for yen and dollars that fail without the guard. | app:actual | Developer accepted the guard; `packages/desktop-client/src/components/util/AmountInput.tsx:135` |
+| PIT003 | Passing an undici Agent (e.g. the SSRF-safe dispatcher) to Node's built-in global fetch in the sync server | The global fetch bundles a different undici version than the installed undici package, so the dispatcher and fetch can mismatch. SimpleFIN bank sync stopped working on a nightly build. | Import fetch from undici in every sync-server module, so the dispatcher and fetch come from the same package. Do not add another HTTP library (axios, node-fetch). In tests, mock undici's fetch, not the global one. | app:actual | Commit 9c300f5 message; developer decision; `packages/sync-server/src/app-simplefin/app-simplefin.js:3` |
+| PIT004 | Comparing a full date string (the stored From) with a bare month or year key (the raw To pick) in custom report range validation | As strings the shorter key sorts before a full date in the same period, so a To in the same month, quarter or year looks reversed and From is reset to the fallback range. | Compare the From date against the normalized end date computed for the interval (validateEnd in reportRanges.ts). Keep tests for the same month, quarter and year. | app:actual | Developer accepted; `packages/desktop-client/src/components/reports/reportRanges.ts:99-103` |
+| PIT005 | Using @zumer/snapdom's toPng result as a download URL (assigning the result directly to link.href) | toPng returns an image element, not a data URL, so the download breaks with no error. | Use the element's src (`link.href = image.src`). | app:actual | Developer statement; `packages/desktop-client/src/components/reports/ReportTopbar.tsx:75-77` |
 
