 Use STACK IDs for evidence-backed entries, with explicit scope. Generated entries require human review. Implementation observations do not establish company policy.
 
 | ID | Decision or constraint | Scope | Rationale | Evidence |
 | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| STACK-001 | Sync server modules import `fetch` from the `undici` package, never Node's global `fetch`. A dispatcher (such as the SimpleFIN SSRF-guarded undici Agent) must be paired with the same undici version's fetch. Do not add another HTTP client library (axios, node-fetch). Tests mock `undici`'s fetch, not the global one. | app:actual (packages/sync-server) | Passing an undici v8 Agent to Node's built-in global fetch, which bundles a different undici version, broke SimpleFIN bank sync. Developer: "I don't want another HTTP library on the server, and undici is what Node ships anyway." | Developer statement; commit 9c300f541fad |
+| STACK-002 | The sync-server package declares `engines.node` as `>=22.19.0`, while the monorepo root stays at `>=22.18.0`. Different floors for root and package are accepted. Do not revert the sync-server floor. | app:actual (packages/sync-server) | Developer decision ("I'm fairly sure that's what we settled on"). The concrete reason was not stated, and no dependency or Node bug in the repo was found that requires 22.19.0. The undici change itself works on any Node 22. | Developer statement; `packages/sync-server/package.json` |
+| STACK-003 | Report image export ("Download Snapshot") uses `@zumer/snapdom`, replacing `html-to-image`. `snapdom.toPng` returns an image element, so use `image.src` as the download href rather than assigning the element to `link.href`. | app:actual (packages/desktop-client) | html-to-image made Download Snapshot fail silently in Firefox. The developer chose snapdom because it is maintained and embeds fonts. The Firefox root cause (font embedding abort) is the developer's belief, not confirmed. | Developer statement; `packages/desktop-client/package.json` |
 
