 Use TERM IDs for evidence-backed entries, with explicit scope. Generated entries require human review. Implementation observations do not establish company policy.
 
 | ID | Term | Meaning | Scope | Evidence |
 | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| TERM-001 | Stored amount scale (integer amount) | Monetary amounts are stored as integers scaled by 100 for every currency, including zero-decimal currencies: 1,500 yen is stored as 150000. A currency's decimal places (decimalPlaces) only affect display and input formatting, never the stored scale. Conversion helpers (amountToInteger, integerToAmount) always use 100. | app:actual | Developer statement; `packages/loot-core/src/shared/util.ts:539` |
+| TERM-002 | Quarterly interval (custom reports) | A custom-report grouping interval. A quarter is keyed by its first month (Q3 2026 is 2026-07) and labelled Q3 '26. Quarters are queried by month and rolled up client-side, the way weeks are rolled up from days, so no AQL changes are needed. Budgeted reports sum the monthly budgeted amounts into the quarter. A From/To pick that is out of range falls back to four whole quarters. NetWorth, BalanceForecast and Spending do not use it. | app:actual | Developer statement; `packages/desktop-client/src/components/reports/reportRanges.ts:27` |
 
